[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"237","stub":{"id":"237","section":"Burrow Valley Road / Sycamore Road to Sycamore Creek","altname":"","river":"Little Dry Creek","difficulty":"IVtoV","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112877","location":{"latitude":"36.9687995910645","longitude":"-119.352699279785"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"118156","location":{"latitude":"36.9235992431641","longitude":"-119.319396972656"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"4","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[],"detail":{"id":"237","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"This run can't really be recommended, but it can be entertaining for locals who want to explore something new near to Fresno during a major rain event.   The creek is tiny so it takes a lot of rain to get it high enough to be boatable.   If everything else is very high then this one might be high enough also.\n\nThere are some major drops in the run, but much of it is also low gradient.   The scenery is of course very nice.\n\nWhen you reach the confluence with Watts Creek there will be a big increase in flow and then again when Sycamore creek enters.    You could walk out at the gauging station just below the confluence with Sycamore, but if you have come that far you might as well salvage something of the day and paddle out [Sycamore Creek— Maxson Road to Trimmer Springs Road](../../content/River_detail_id_309_), which really is quite fun at high flows.","averageGradient":"0","maxGradient":"0","length":"4.5","correlations":[],"pointOfInterestIDs":["112877","118156"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-119.35304859184716,36.9682678759512],[-119.35289599184738,36.968111475951446],[-119.35268252518108,36.96787880928514],[-119.352529791848,36.967768075951994],[-119.35236179184825,36.96772607595204